{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"The upagrahas of BPHS ch. 3. Five from the Sun (st. 61-64): Dhuma (Sun + 133\u00b020'), Vyatipata (360\u00b0 - Dhuma), Parivesha (Vyatipata + 180\u00b0), Indrachapa (360\u00b0 - Parivesha), Upaketu (Indrachapa + 16\u00b040', one sign behind the Sun). Five that rise in the eight parts of the day or night, counted from the weekday lord by day and from the fifth lord by night (st. 66-70): Kala (Sun's part), Mrityu (Mars), Ardhaprahara (Mercury), Yamaghantaka (Jupiter), Gulika (Saturn), each as the sidereal lagna at the start of its part with the end beside it. Mandi by the ghatika table of the Prasna Marga notes.\n\n[Group: Vedic]\n[Endpoint: POST /v1/vedic/upagrahas]\n[Required: date, time, latitude, longitude]\n[Cost: 20 credits (Tier 2)]","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"ayanamsa":{"description":"Sidereal school by name. Lahiri when omitted. Equivalent to ayanamsaId; send either.","enum":["fagan-bradley","lahiri","de-luce","raman","krishnamurti","kp","yukteshwar","jn-bhasin","true-citra","djwhal-khul"],"type":"string"},"ayanamsaId":{"type":["number","null"]},"city":{"default":"","type":"string"},"cosmogram":{"type":"boolean"},"date":{"pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"houseSystem":{"default":"P","enum":["P","K","R","C","E","W","B","M","O","A","T","V","D","F","G","H","I","i","L","N","Q","S","U","X","Y"],"type":"string"},"latitude":{"maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"type":"number"},"longitude":{"maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"},"name":{"default":"","type":"string"},"time":{"pattern":"^\\d{2}:\\d{2}(:\\d{2})?$","type":"string"},"timezone":{"description":"IANA zone name such as Europe/Kyiv, or auto to look the zone up from latitude and longitude. The server takes the offset that zone kept at this local date and time, summer time included, an